@startuml async-detached-driver
' ============================================================================
' The tokio "fire-and-forget" family: what was NOT fire-and-forget before, and
' what the repair changed.  TWO distinct resources are at stake and the figure
' keeps them apart:
'   RED  #C62828 native stack (nested `poll`)   BLUE #1565C0 heap (parked futures)
'   GREEN #2E7D32 the repair                    TEAL #00695C the completion counter
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4

title <b>Detached-spawn + atomic-counter reduction driver</b>\ntwo resources, two defects, one repair

package "**BEFORE** — two separate <latex>\Theta(N)</latex> chains on one path" as BEF #FFEBEE {

  rectangle "**(i) NESTED `poll` — native stack**\n`eval` → `produce`/`consume` → `dispatch` → `eval`\nawaited **inline** through `Box::pin`, so polling the\nouter future polls the inner one **in the same frame**" as I #FFCDD2
  rectangle "the mitigation that was shipped:\n`StackGrowingFuture` + `stacker::maybe_grow`\n`STACK_RED_ZONE = 1 MiB`, `STACK_GROW_SIZE = 2 MiB`\n<i>grows the stack instead of not needing it</i>" as IM #EF9A9A

  rectangle "**(ii) PARKED-PARENT CHAIN — heap**\neach parent `await`s its children, so every ancestor's\nfuture stays **live and parked** until the whole\nsubtree finishes.  `shortslow.rho`: **32,768 parked parents**" as II #BBDEFB

  I -[#C62828,thickness=2]-> IM : guarded by
  note bottom of IM #FFF3E0
    f1r3node issues **#305** and **#306**
  end note
}

package "**AFTER** — one <latex>O(1)</latex>-frame task per branch, joined by a counter" as AFT #E8F5E9 {

  rectangle "`inj` seeds a per-deploy **`DriveState`**\n`live: AtomicUsize` (init **1** = the root eval)\n`sink: Mutex<Vec<InterpreterError>>`\n`done: oneshot::Sender<()>`" as D #80CBC4

  rectangle "**`spawn_detached(drive, path, fut)`**\n1. `live.fetch_add(1, AcqRel)`  ← **increment BEFORE spawn**\n2. `tokio::spawn(async move { … })`  ← the parent does **not** await\n3. inside: `LiveGuard` (RAII decrement) dropped **last**\n4. `AssertUnwindSafe(fut).catch_unwind().await`\n5. `Err` / panic → `Located { path, source }` into `sink`" as S #A5D6A7

  rectangle "**`LiveGuard::drop`**\n`if live.fetch_sub(1, AcqRel) == 1 { done.send(()) }`\n⇒ fires **exactly once**, on the <latex>1 \rightarrow 0</latex> transition" as G #A5D6A7

  rectangle "`inj` drops the root guard, `await`s the oneshot,\nthen sorts `sink` by `located_path` for a deterministic\n**display** order (explicitly **not** consensus)" as J #80CBC4

  D -[#2E7D32,thickness=2]-> S
  S -[#2E7D32,thickness=2]-> G
  G -[#2E7D32,thickness=2]-> J
}

BEF -[#455A64,thickness=3]right-> AFT : five join sites detached\n(Site 1 = `eval_inner`'s parallel join;\nSites 2–5 = `run_parallel_dispatches`)

note bottom of AFT #E8F5E9
  ★ **The stack-safety connection, stated precisely.**  `tokio::spawn` roots a task on its own
  stack, so a spawned-and-awaited child does **not** nest `poll` frames — resource (i) is fixed by
  the fact that the recursion is now *spawned* rather than *inlined*.  Resource (ii) is **heap**, not
  stack: <latex>N</latex> parked parents are <latex>\Theta(N)</latex> live future objects, not
  <latex>\Theta(N)</latex> frames.  Detaching removes both, and `StackGrowingFuture` +
  the `stacker` dependency were then **deleted** rather than retuned.
end note

note bottom of BEF #FFF3E0
  ⚠ **What "fire-and-forget" does *not* mean here.**  The child is not unobserved: completion is
  tracked by the counter and errors by the sink.  What is given up is the **parent's `await`** —
  i.e. the structural coupling of a send to its continuation — which is what Rholang's asynchronous
  send always meant semantically.  Concurrency is unchanged (the same spawns), so COMM order is
  unchanged, which is the consensus-neutrality argument.
end note

@enduml
